{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771200847918,"sessionID":"ses_39c3416c0ffeUYCFcwGrAdjGPB","part":{"id":"prt_c63cc1ff3001BTptF59yCPZHFc","sessionID":"ses_39c3416c0ffeUYCFcwGrAdjGPB","messageID":"msg_c63cbff57001pMoBq7mwMwcKwB","type":"tool","callID":"call_df6620c5409b421485f0d2c3","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/expert-settings.md"},"output":"<path>/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/expert-settings.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>1: # Spec: Expert Settings / Dev Panel\n2: \n3: ## Overview\n4: Hidden configuration interface for tuning game mechanics, balancing parameters, and debugging. Accessible during development and for advanced users to find optimal parametrization.\n5: \n6: ## Functional Requirements\n7: \n8: ### Access Methods\n9: ```typescript\n10: interface ExpertSettingsAccess {\n11:   keyboardShortcut: string;      // '`' (backtick) for quick access\n12:   menuPath: string;              // \"Settings → Advanced → Expert Mode\" (if menu system exists)\n13:   gesture: string;               // Mobile: triple-tap top-left corner\n14: }\n15: ```\n16: \n17: ### Configurable Parameters\n18: \n19: #### Movement Detection Parameters\n20: ```typescript\n21: interface MovementDetectionParams {\n22:   centroidHistoryLength: number;       // Generations to track (default: 5, range: 3-10)\n23:   movementThreshold: number;           // Cells to be \"moving\" (default: 0.5, range: 0.1-2.0)\n24:   minClusterSize: number;            // Minimum cells to track (default: 1, range: 1-5)\n25: }\n26: ```\n27: \n28: #### Scoring Parameters\n29: ```typescript\n30: interface ScoringParams {\n31:   moverPointsPerGeneration: number;      // Default: 10, range: 1-100\n32:   oscillatorPointsPerGeneration: number;   // Default: 2, range: 0-20\n33:   scoreMultiplier: number;                // Default: 1.0, range: 0.1-5.0\n34: }\n35: ```\n36: \n37: #### Level Generation Parameters\n38: ```typescript\n39: interface LevelGenerationParams {\n40:   baseTimeSeconds: number;                // Default: 45, range: 10-120\n41:   timeIncrementPerLevel: number;          // Default: 15, range: 0-60\n42:   baseFlux: number;                       // Default: 20, range: 5-50\n43:   difficultyScalingMode: 'TIME_ONLY' | 'RESOURCE_ONLY' | 'MIXED' | 'EXTREME';\n44: }\n45: ```\n46: \n47: #### Grid Sizing Parameters\n48: ```typescript\n49: interface GridSizingParams {\n50:   mobileCellSize: number;                 // Default: 18, range: 14-24\n51:   desktopCellSize: number;                // Default: 20, range: 16-28\n52:   minVisibleCells: number;                // Default: 10, minimum cells visible\n53: }\n54: ```\n55: \n56: ### Settings Persistence\n57: - Save to localStorage under key `gol-expert-settings`\n58: - Load on app startup\n59: - \"Reset to Defaults\" button with confirmation\n60: - Export/Import settings as JSON (for sharing configurations)\n61: \n62: ## UI/UX Requirements\n63: \n64: ### Panel Layout\n65: - **Position**: Modal overlay, centered or right sidebar\n66: - **Sections**: Collapsible groups by category (Movement, Scoring, Levels, Grid)\n67: - **Controls**:\n68:   - Sliders for numeric ranges\n69:   - Number inputs for precise values\n70:   - Dropdowns for mode selection\n71: \n72: ### Real-Time Updates\n73: - Changes apply immediately (no restart required)\n74: - Visual indicator when value differs from default\n75: - \"Revert\" button per section\n76: - Live preview: Show parameter effects in real-time if possible\n77: \n78: ### Danger Zone\n79: - Separate section for \"Break Things\" settings\n80: - Require confirmation for extreme values\n81: - Show warning if settings would make game impossible\n82: \n83: ### Export/Import\n84: - \"Export JSON\" button downloads current config\n85: - \"Import JSON\" file picker loads config\n86: - Validate imported JSON against schema\n87: \n88: ## Edge Cases\n89: \n90: 1. **Invalid Values**: Input validation prevents negative numbers, out-of-range values\n91: 2. **Settings While Running**: Changes to scoring apply immediately; level changes apply on next level\n92: 3. **Reset During Game**: Reset to defaults should warn if game in progress\n93: 4. **Corrupted Storage**: If localStorage has invalid JSON, fall back to defaults\n94: 5. **Mobile Access**: Ensure gesture detection doesn't conflict with game controls\n95: \n96: ## Implementation Notes\n97: \n98: - Use React Context or Zustand for settings state\n99: - Validate all inputs with constraints\n100: - Schema validation using Zod or similar\n101: - Default values should create balanced, playable game\n102: - Consider \"Presets\" dropdown (\"Easy\", \"Normal\", \"Hard\", \"Chaos\")\n103: - Expert settings should be accessible but not intrusive\n104: - Document each parameter with tooltip explaining its effect\n105: \n\n(End of file - total 105 lines)\n</content>","title":"specs/expert-settings.md","metadata":{"preview":"# Spec: Expert Settings / Dev Panel\n\n## Overview\nHidden configuration interface for tuning game mechanics, balancing parameters, and debugging. Accessible during development and for advanced users to find optimal parametrization.\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n### Access Methods\n```typescript\ninterface ExpertSettingsAccess {\n  keyboardShortcut: string;      // '`' (backtick) for quick access\n  menuPath: string;              // \"Settings → Advanced → Expert Mode\" (if menu system exists)\n  gesture: string;               // Mobile: triple-tap top-left corner\n}\n```\n\n### Configurable Parameters\n\n#### Movement Detection Parameters\n```typescript","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"time":{"start":1771200847862,"end":1771200847916}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771200893088,"sessionID":"ses_39c3416c0ffeUYCFcwGrAdjGPB","part":{"id":"prt_c63cc1ff9001w4XhpmMzElZeyY","sessionID":"ses_39c3416c0ffeUYCFcwGrAdjGPB","messageID":"msg_c63cbff57001pMoBq7mwMwcKwB","type":"tool","callID":"call_f2e66be6574240c1a6a56dd6","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Study specs files comprehensively","subagent_type":"explore","prompt":"Read ALL spec files in specs/ directory to understand the application specifications. Provide a comprehensive summary of each spec file's key requirements, particularly focusing on what's NOT yet implemented based on IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md."},"output":"task_id: ses_39c33dffbffe7VnQQ3WbXb24UE (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\nNow I'll analyze all the spec files against the IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md to identify what's not yet implemented:\n\n---\n\n# Comprehensive Analysis: Spec Files vs Implementation Status\n\nBased on reviewing all 13 spec files and the IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md, here's a comprehensive summary of what's NOT yet implemented:\n\n---\n\n## 1. **auto-advance-transitions.md** ✅ MOSTLY COMPLETE\n**Status:** Transitions implemented, minor edge cases verified\n\n**WHAT IS IMPLEMENTED:**\n- All 5 transition states (PLAYING, FADING_OUT, INTERSTITIAL, FADING_IN, READY)\n- Skip functionality with Space/ESC keys\n- Configurable durations (2.0s for each phase)\n- Browser tab handling (pause transitions when tab inactive)\n- Interstitial display with level numbers\n\n**NOT YET IMPLEMENTED:**\n- **None** - This spec is fully implemented\n\n---\n\n## 2. **expert-settings.md** ⚠️ PARTIAL\n**Status:** SettingsPanel exists, but missing many expert features\n\n**WHAT IS IMPLEMENTED:**\n- SettingsPanel component with collapsible sections\n- Basic controls for: audio, movement detection, scoring, level generation, grid sizing\n- Settings persistence to localStorage\n- Reset to defaults functionality\n- Parameter validation\n\n**NOT YET IMPLEMENTED:**\n- **Alternative access methods** (backtick shortcut ``, triple-tap mobile gesture)\n- **Export/Import JSON** functionality for sharing configurations\n- **Danger Zone** section for extreme settings with warnings\n- **Visual indicators** when values differ from defaults\n- **Per-section Revert** buttons\n- **Live preview** of parameter effects\n- **Comprehensive tooltips** explaining each parameter's effect\n- **Presets dropdown** (Easy, Normal, Hard, Chaos) - see specs/presets-system\n- **Schema validation** using Zod or similar library\n- **Export/Import** JSON for configuration sharing\n\n---\n\n## 3. **level-progression.md** ✅ COMPLETE\n**Status:** Fully implemented\n\n**WHAT IS IMPLEMENTED:**\n- LevelConfig interface with levelNumber, timeLimitSeconds, initialFlux\n- All 4 difficulty scaling strategies (TIME_ONLY, RESOURCE_ONLY, MIXED, EXTREME)\n- Progression state with currentLevel, maxUnlockedLevel, totalScore\n- 10-level progression system\n- Victory screen after final level\n- \"Level X\" display in title\n- localStorage persistence\n\n**NOT YET IMPLEMENTED:**\n- **None** - This spec is fully implemented\n\n---\n\n## 4. **user-interaction.md** ✅ COMPLETE\n**Status:** Fully implemented\n\n**WHAT IS IMPLEMENTED:**\n- Mouse interaction (down, move, up events)\n- Touch interaction with preventDefault for all events\n- Coordinate mapping to grid cells\n- Drag-to-draw support\n- DRAW and ERASE modes\n- Boundary handling\n\n**NOT YET IMPLEMENTED:**\n- **None** - This spec is fully implemented\n\n---\n\n## 5. **grid-interaction.md** ✅ COMPLETE\n**Status:** Fully implemented\n\n**WHAT IS IMPLEMENTED:**\n- Click-to-place/erase functionality\n- Cell preview ghost outline on hover\n- Cursor states (crosshair, forbidden symbol, minus icon)\n- Fade-in and shrink animations for cells\n- Red flash for invalid actions\n- Minimum cells rule (START disabled until ≥1 cell placed)\n- Phase-based interaction constraints\n\n**NOT YET IMPLEMENTED:**\n- **None** - This spec is fully implemented\n\n---\n\n## 6. **ui-overlay.md** ✅ COMPLETE\n**Status:** Fully implemented\n\n**WHAT IS IMPLEMENTED:**\n- Cinematic IntroOverlay with glitch effect and attract mode\n- Glass HUD container with glassmorphism styling\n- Main control buttons (PLAY/PAUSE, STEP, RANDOM, CLEAR)\n- Interaction mode buttons (DRAW, ERASE)\n- Waveform selector and volume slider\n- Generation counter display\n- Phase status display (PLANNING, COUNTDOWN, RUNNING, FINISHED)\n- Settings panel with gear icon access\n- UI toggle button for show/hide functionality\n\n**NOT YET IMPLEMENTED:**\n- **None** - This spec is fully implemented\n\n---\n\n## 7. **phase-management.md** ✅ COMPLETE\n**Status:** Fully implemented\n\n**WHAT IS IMPLEMENTED:**\n- Phase state machine with 4 phases (PLANNING, COUNTDOWN, RUNNING, FINISHED)\n- Guarded transitions with blockers\n- Countdown timer (3, 2, 1...)\n- RUNNING phase timer with level-specific duration\n- FINISHED phase delay before transition\n- Phase guard conditions (START disabled until ≥1 cell)\n- Browser tab handling (timer continues during gameplay, pauses during transitions)\n\n**NOT YET IMPLEMENTED:**\n- **None** - This spec is fully implemented\n\n---\n\n## 8. **scoring-system.md** ⚠️ PARTIAL\n**Status:** Core scoring implemented, missing UI features\n\n**WHAT IS IMPLEMENTED:**\n- Per-generation scoring based on cluster classifications\n- MOVER: 10 points/gen, OSCILLATOR: 2 points/gen, STATIC: 0\n- Score multiplier support\n- Score cap at MAX_SAFE_INTEGER\n- ScoreDisplay component with PTS label\n- Smooth increment animation with lerp\n- Pulse animation on point gain\n- Milestone flash every 100 points\n- Score resets per level\n\n**NOT YET IMPLEMENTED:**\n- **Pattern breakdown UI** (Active Movers count, Active Oscillators count, Current rate in points/gen) - marked as optional but in spec\n- **End-of-level stats** (Final score, Time survived, Patterns created)\n- **High score persistence** to localStorage (save highest score per level, display on UI)\n\n---\n\n## 9. **movement-detection.md** ✅ COMPLETE\n**Status:** Fully implemented\n\n**WHAT IS IMPLEMENTED:**\n- Connected component detection using BFS with 8-connectivity\n- Centroid tracking with configurable history length\n- Velocity calculation across history\n- Cluster classification (MOVER, OSCILLATOR, STATIC)\n- Cluster matching across generations\n- Handling of edge cases (splits, merges, single cells)\n- Performance optimizations (target < 16ms for 60fps)\n\n**NOT YET IMPLEMENTED:**\n- **None** - This spec is fully implemented\n\n---\n\n## 10. **canvas-rendering.md** ✅ COMPLETE\n**Status:** Fully implemented\n\n**WHAT IS IMPLEMENTED:**\n- Canvas setup with DPR scaling for sharp rendering\n- Age-based cell colors (cyan, blue, magenta, purple)\n- Glow effects based on cell age\n- Grid lines toggle (G key, only during PLANNING)\n- Responsive cell sizing (18px mobile, 20px desktop)\n- Window resize handling\n- Square cells with 2px corner radius\n- Intensity metric (--life-intensity CSS variable)\n- Optimized rendering pipeline\n\n**NOT YET IMPLEMENTED:**\n- **None** - This spec is fully implemented\n\n---\n\n## 11. **audio-sonification.md** ✅ COMPLETE\n**Status:** Fully implemented\n\n**WHAT IS IMPLEMENTED:**\n- SoundEngine class with Web Audio API\n- Lazy initialization for AudioContext\n- Generation sounds with pitch mapping based on row position\n- Interaction sounds (draw: 880Hz, erase: 440Hz)\n- Simulation start sound\n- Level complete sound\n- Level start sound\n- Transition whoosh sound\n- Insufficient flux error sound\n- Volume control (0.0-0.5)\n- Waveform selection (sine, triangle, square, sawtooth)\n- Enable/disable toggle\n- Polyphonic support\n\n**NOT YET IMPLEMENTED:**\n- **None** - This spec is fully implemented\n\n---\n\n## 12. **simulation-engine.md** ✅ COMPLETE\n**Status:** Fully implemented\n\n**WHAT IS IMPLEMENTED:**\n- RuleSet interface with born/survive arrays\n- Conway's rules: born=[3], survive=[2,3]\n- Neighbor counting with Moore neighborhood\n- Toroidal boundary handling (wrap edges with modulo)\n- Age tracking for cells\n- Double-buffer pattern for state updates\n- Performance optimizations (React ref, precomputed offsets)\n- Generation counter\n- Grid resizing support (Small: 20×30, Medium: 40×50, Large: 60×80)\n- Birth statistics tracking (born count, average row position)\n\n**NOT YET IMPLEMENTED:**\n- **None** - This spec is fully implemented\n\n---\n\n## 13. **flux-management.md** ⚠️ PARTIAL\n**Status:** Core mechanics implemented, audio feedback missing\n\n**WHAT IS IMPLEMENTED:**\n- Flux state with current, initial, placed, removed tracking\n- Placement cost (1 Flux per cell)\n- Refund mechanic during PLANNING phase\n- No refunds during RUNNING phase\n- Play phase placement using saved Flux\n- FluxDisplay component with smooth animations\n- Color coding (green/yellow when >30%, orange when <30%, red when 0)\n- Flux counter resets per level\n\n**NOT YET IMPLEMENTED:**\n- **Audio feedback** for Flux actions:\n  - Placement: soft \"plop\" sound\n  - Insufficient Flux: error/denied sound (actually, flux error sound IS implemented in SoundEngine, but marked as pending in IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md)\n  - Removal: suction/remove sound\n\n---\n\n# Summary: What's NOT Yet Implemented\n\n## CRITICAL GAPS (Blocking Features)\n\n**None** - All critical features are implemented. The application is fully playable.\n\n## MEDIUM PRIORITY GAPS (Enhancements)\n\n1. **Scoring System UI Enhancements** (`specs/scoring-system.md`):\n   - Pattern breakdown UI showing active movers/oscillators and current rate\n   - End-of-level stats display (final score, time survived, patterns created)\n   - High score persistence to localStorage with UI display\n\n2. **Flux Audio Feedback** (`specs/flux-management.md`):\n   - Actually implemented in SoundEngine (flux error sound), but marked as pending in plan\n   - Need to verify placement and removal sounds are connected\n\n3. **Mobile Visual Feedback** (`specs/ui-overlay.md`):\n   - Touch ripple effect on button interactions\n   - Mobile expert settings access via triple-tap gesture\n\n## LOW PRIORITY GAPS (Polish & Convenience)\n\n4. **Expert Settings Advanced Features** (`specs/expert-settings.md`):\n   - Backtick keyboard shortcut (`) access\n   - Triple-tap mobile gesture for access\n   - Export/Import JSON configuration\n   - Danger Zone section with extreme settings and warnings\n   - Visual indicators when values differ from defaults\n   - Per-section Revert buttons\n   - Live preview of parameter effects\n   - Comprehensive tooltips for each parameter\n   - Presets dropdown (Easy, Normal, Hard, Chaos)\n   - Schema validation using Zod\n\n5. **Quality Assurance** (Sprint 6 - not yet started):\n   - Global error boundary for React\n   - Comprehensive input validation\n   - Edge case handling improvements\n   - Retry mechanisms for failed operations\n   - Browser compatibility checks with fallbacks\n   - Keyboard navigation for grid (arrow keys, Enter/Space)\n   - Screen reader support (ARIA labels, live regions)\n   - Reduced motion support (prefers-reduced-motion)\n   - High contrast mode toggle\n   - Focus management in modals\n   - Performance monitoring (FPS counter, profiling)\n   - Performance optimizations (memoization, virtualization)\n   - Lazy loading for non-critical components\n   - Comprehensive unit and integration tests\n\n---\n\n# Overall Assessment\n\n**Implementation Status: ~85% Complete**\n\nThe application is **fully playable** with all core mechanics, game loop, and UI implemented. The missing features are primarily:\n- **Visual polish** (touch ripple, mobile gestures)\n- **Convenience features** (presets, export/import)\n- **Accessibility features** (keyboard nav, screen reader)\n- **Quality assurance** (error handling, testing, performance monitoring)\n\n**Key Specs Fully Implemented:**\n- ✅ simulation-engine.md\n- ✅ canvas-rendering.md\n- ✅ user-interaction.md\n- ✅ grid-interaction.md\n- ✅ flux-management.md (core)\n- ✅ phase-management.md\n- ✅ ui-overlay.md\n- ✅ movement-detection.md\n- ✅ scoring-system.md (core)\n- ✅ level-progression.md\n- ✅ auto-advance-transitions.md\n- ✅ audio-sonification.md\n\n**Key Specs Partially Implemented:**\n- ⚠️ expert-settings.md (missing advanced features)\n- ⚠️ scoring-system.md (missing UI breakdown and high score)\n- ⚠️ flux-management.md (some audio feedback may be missing)\n\n**Not Yet Started:**\n- ❌ Accessibility (Sprint 6.2)\n- ❌ Performance Optimization (Sprint 6.3)\n- ❌ Testing (Sprint 6.4)\n- ❌ Error Handling & Resilience (Sprint 6.1)\n</task_result>","title":"Study specs files comprehensively","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_39c33dffbffe7VnQQ3WbXb24UE","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771200847872,"end":1771200893085}}}}
